Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 20:44:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: publish the power-plan finding as F-12, and bind the
 bench protocol to it

The President ruled this ships with the fork; 110F flagged that nobody had
confirmed it reached the docs. It had not. Verified absent, now folded.

F-12 records the whole thing: decode 29.3 -> 11.2 under a third-party
"performance" power plan, the bisection showing every single-variable arm
innocent (min-processor-100% 29.0, AMD slider 28.8) and only the pair
collapsing (14.5, verbatim plan 11.2), and the shared-package-budget
mechanism that explains why the same plan makes CPU-bound work ~4x faster.

The four-plan comparison is included because the obvious objection is that
Balanced was merely lucky: Balanced 29.12/28.95, Ultimate 28.90, High
Performance 28.39, the optimizer's plan 11.07, same box and hour and command.
Numbers taken from the register row that owns this issue, not from a prose
retelling of it.

Protocol changes that follow, in the same unit of work:
- CHANGELOG gains a third standing rule: every performance claim was taken
  under the declared power plan.
- OPTIONS-REGISTRY says so in its preamble, because every default in it was
  chosen under Balanced and a re-measurement under another plan is not a
  comparison.
- FINDINGS' "How we measure" now names the plan alongside the hardware.

Origin: lane-110G, publication mandate - the President ruled this finding ships
  with the fork, and 110F flagged that nobody had confirmed it reached the docs.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED by this commit - documentation only. The figures it
  publishes were measured 2026-07-29 and are taken from the register row that
  owns the issue rather than from a prose retelling of it.
